invariant: INV-14
file: srv_auth.c
catches: srv_auth_test
reason: srv_identities_usable stops asking p256_sign_key_ok, so a
  server starts a session with an ECDSA scalar of 0 or of the group
  order, which p256_sign refuses inside the flight after the ServerHello
  went out. test/srv_identity_tests.h requires both scalars to be
  refused by the check and by ch_srv_accept before any I/O.

--- old
    if (sigalg == SIGALG_ECDSA_P256_SHA256) {
        return p256_sign_key_ok(id->priv);
    }
--- new
    if (sigalg == SIGALG_ECDSA_P256_SHA256) {
        return 1;
    }
